  "name": "Fear of Disappointment",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-eye.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The weight of expectation causes your allies to perform. You can spend an action and expend 1 link depth from the link of a linked creature to grant them advantage on all attacks until the start of your next turn. You can spend additional link depth when activating this feature; if you do, the linked creature also deals additional psychic damage on attacks equal to twice the number of additional link depth expended. If they attack a linked creature the additional damage is quadrupled instead.</p><p><a href=\"https://dnd-wiki.org/wiki/Empath_(5e_Class)\">Source: Empath by Axis, co-authored by Ghostwheel</a> (CC BY-SA 3.0). See the module's AUTOMATION.md for what is automated and how rules are interpreted.</p>",
